This repository holds three different things under three different terms. The
split matters: a permissive licence over the whole repository would hand anybody
who reads it a licence to use the logo, which is the opposite of what a logo is
for.

## The build is Apache-2.0

`src/`, `gates/`, `tools/`, `kagami.config.mjs` and the workflows are ordinary
code, licensed under the Apache License 2.0 in `LICENSE`. Take it, adapt it,
point it at your own mark.

Apache-2.0 was chosen over MIT for section 6, which says in the licence itself
that it grants no trademark rights. That is the exact sentence this repository
needs, so it does not have to be bolted on beside a licence that is silent.

## The marks are not licensed to anybody

Everything under `dist/`, `init/`, `baselines/` and `brand/marks/`, and every
value in `brand/tokens/color.json`, is the WavingEye visual identity. It is a
trademark. Reading this repository grants no permission to use it, reproduce it,
or make a derivative of it, and Apache-2.0 section 6 says so explicitly.

Being able to fetch a file is not permission to use it. The files are public so
that WavingEye's own projects can install them and so that anybody working with
WavingEye can be handed a URL instead of a zip.

## Montserrat is OFL 1.1

`brand/fonts/Montserrat[wght].ttf` is Montserrat, copyright the Montserrat
Project Authors, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Its text is in
`brand/fonts/OFL.txt`. The OFL permits the use made of it here, including
setting a wordmark in it and shipping outlines of that wordmark.

The wordmark's *letterforms* are Montserrat's and are OFL. The wordmark as a
mark of WavingEye is not.
